```apex
public class LeadImportService with sharing {

    public class ImportResult {
        public Integer successCount { get; }
        public List<Id> insertedIds { get; }
        public Map<Integer, String> errorsByIndex { get; }

        public ImportResult(Integer successCount, List<Id> insertedIds, Map<Integer, String> errorsByIndex) {
            this.successCount = successCount;
            this.insertedIds = insertedIds;
            this.errorsByIndex = errorsByIndex;
        }
    }

    public static ImportResult importLeads(List<Lead> leads) {
        // Null or empty input
        if (leads == null || leads.isEmpty()) {
            return new ImportResult(0, new List<Id>(), new Map<Integer, String>());
        }

        Set<String> seenEmails = new Set<String>();
        Map<Integer, String> duplicateErrors = new Map<Integer, String>();
        List<Lead> leadsToInsert = new List<Lead>();
        List<Integer> originalIndices = new List<Integer>(); // parallel to leadsToInsert

        for (Integer i = 0; i < leads.size(); i++) {
            Lead lead = leads[i];

            // Set LeadSource to 'Web' if blank
            if (lead != null && String.isBlank(lead.LeadSource)) {
                lead.LeadSource = 'Web';
            }

            // Duplicate email detection (case-insensitive, trimmed)
            if (lead != null && !String.isBlank(lead.Email)) {
                String normalizedEmail = lead.Email.trim().toLowerCase();
                if (seenEmails.contains(normalizedEmail)) {
                    duplicateErrors.put(i, 'Duplicate email in import: ' + normalizedEmail);
                    continue; // exclude from DML
                }
                seenEmails.add(normalizedEmail);
            }

            originalIndices.add(i);
            leadsToInsert.add(lead);
        }

        // Single DML statement
        List<Database.SaveResult> results;
        if (leadsToInsert.isEmpty()) {
            results = new List<Database.SaveResult>();
        } else {
            results = Database.insert(leadsToInsert, false);
        }

        // Build result
        Map<Integer, String> errorsByIndex = new Map<Integer, String>();
        for (Integer idx : duplicateErrors.keySet()) {
            errorsByIndex.put(idx, duplicateErrors.get(idx));
        }

        List<Id> insertedIds = new List<Id>();
        Integer successCount = 0;

        for (Integer j = 0; j < results.size(); j++) {
            Database.SaveResult sr = results[j];
            Integer originalIdx = originalIndices.get(j);

            if (sr.isSuccess()) {
                insertedIds.add(sr.getId());
                successCount++;
            } else {
                List<String> messages = new List<String>();
                for (Database.Error err : sr.getErrors()) {
                    messages.add(err.getMessage());
                }
                errorsByIndex.put(originalIdx, String.join(messages, '; '));
            }
        }

        return new ImportResult(successCount, insertedIds, errorsByIndex);
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

1. **`with sharing`** on the class ensures the running user's sharing rules are respected for the DML.

2. **Single DML** — all non-duplicate leads are collected into one list and inserted via a single `Database.insert(leadsToInsert, false)` call. The `false` flag means one bad record won't roll back the others.

3. **Duplicate detection** happens *before* DML, so duplicate leads are never sent to the database. The first occurrence "claims" the email in `seenEmails`; subsequent occurrences are filtered out and recorded in `errorsByIndex` directly. This means the duplicate rule applies regardless of whether the first lead ultimately succeeds or fails at the database level.

4. **Order preservation** — `originalIndices` is a parallel list to `leadsToInsert`, so we can map each `SaveResult` back to the caller's 0-based input position. Since we iterate in order, `insertedIds` is naturally in input order.

5. **Null-lead safety** — a null entry in the input list is guarded against for the `LeadSource`/`Email` mutations and will flow through to DML where the platform rejects it with its own error message.

